# lf123, the grandmother-judging swineherd (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf123
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_ragnar_wetby
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the grandmother-judging swineherd
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk has_opinions_about_everyone_s_grandmother
likes smoked_eel singing full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes early_bells stale_bread
fears a_piglet_lost_to_the_wood a_question_about_the_city_trip
hopes a_full_larder_for_the_house a_good_song_after_the_herd_is_fed
topics work +0.4 family +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=frank gossip=blunt refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tends the #pigs#, sings while filling the #trough#, and offers unsolicited judgments about every #grandmother# in town.

words
oath! = Pig and frost | By the good old grandmothers
saying! = A grandmother sees the missing pig first | Feed the herd before the song
pig = pig | yard pig
pigs = pigs | Southwood pigs
piglet = piglet | young piglet
piglets = piglets | young piglets
sow = sow | older sow
boar = boar | stubborn boar
yard = yard | pig yard
pen = pen | fenced pen
pens = pens | fenced pens
gate = gate | yard gate
latch = latch | gate latch
fence = fence | low fence
trough = trough | feed trough
troughs = troughs | full troughs
feed = feed | mixed feed
grain = grain | dry grain
straw = straw | clean straw
mud = mud | yard mud
hoof = hoof | small hoof
hooves = hooves | muddy hooves
herd = herd | small herd
hand = hand | yard hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | yard work
lesson = lesson | herding lesson
master = master | older herder
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
newcomer = newcomer | newcomer to town
grandmother = grandmother | old grandmother
grandmothers = grandmothers | town grandmothers
family = family | house family
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | cottage door
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof
larder = larder | full larder
bread = bread | day bread
loaf = loaf | stale loaf
eel = eel | smoked eel
plate = plate | supper plate
meal = meal | evening meal
song = song | yard song
songs = songs | old songs
singing = singing | quiet singing
voice = voice | young voice
chorus = chorus | familiar chorus
bell = bell | early bell
bells = bells | early bells
morning = morning | frosty morning
frost = frost | white frost
cold = cold | morning cold
night = night | quiet night
evening = evening | late evening
day = day | working day
field = field | near field
wood = wood | Southwood wood
road = road | long road
path = path | field path
cart = cart | feed cart
wagon = wagon | goods wagon
city = city | far city
market = market | town market
merchant = merchant | market merchant
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | spare coin
festival = festival | town festival
music = music | festival music
sweet = sweet | festival sweet
sweets = sweets | festival sweets
watch = watch | town watch
queue = queue | market queue
snow = snow | first snow
rain = rain | cold rain
wind = wind | field wind
boot = boot | work boot
bucket = bucket | feed bucket
boots = boots | work boots
walk = walk | short walk
orchard = orchard | nearby orchard
visitor = visitor | passing visitor

any
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #festival# has #sweets# and #music# after the #pigs# are fed. | No one hurries me home from it.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A #merchant# adds a #coin# to the #price# when folk stop counting. | I count even for a #loaf#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Another #hand# in the #yard# means less work to learn for me. | I want to know what they can do first.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #feed# costs more and the #larder# fills more slowly. | A #pig# notices an empty #trough#.
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : There are things to see in the #city#. | I do not have a story about my last trip.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A #road# can take a #cart# farther than I wish to go. | I like the #field# #path#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# may know a new #song#. | They can stay outside the #gate# until I finish the #feed#.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : I have heard a #grandmother# in a great #house# knows every worker by sight. | I would like to see if that is true.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #troughs# are nearly full. | #greet#. Did you hear my #song# from the #road#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come see the new #piglet#. | I kept you the better piece of #eel#.
line @1 greet.return : The #sow# has stayed in her #pen# since you left. | You missed the best part of the #chorus#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There is #bread# at the #house#. | After supper, come find the #piglets# with me.
line @1 again.open : I was telling you what a #grandmother# would say. | Did the #boar# get into that #pen#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have #feed# to carry. | Mind the #latch# at the #gate#.
line @1 farewell.return : Next time I may know another #song#. | The #piglets# will be bigger by then.
line @1 react.news : Tell me who said it. | This #trough# will take its #feed# while you speak.
line @1 react.news.new : That is new to this #yard#. | Who brought it from the #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : Someone in the #house# mentioned it. | Your account gives the rest.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would ask who counted the #pigs#. | Which #hand# stood by the #gate# that #day#?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is painful news; the #feed# can stay in its #bucket#. | Come under the #roof#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good; that calls for a #song#. | I will save you the last #sweet#.
line @1 answer.how : The #pigs# are fed and the #frost# is lifting. | I have had a full #plate# today.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am carrying this #feed# to the #pens#. | Let me close the #gate# first.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #bells# wake you too early? | Have you eaten any #eel# today?
line @1 sympathise : I can share the #bread# in our #house#. | Sit until the #wind# settles.
line @1 reassure : We can follow the #hooves# before the #frost# melts. | The #larder# has enough for tonight.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave the #piglets# in an open #pen#. | I will not speak about that #city# trip.
line @1 accept_decline : All right; I will keep the #feed# here. | Then let the #song# wait.
line @1 thank : You closed the #gate# before the #boar# moved. | That #eel# was worth the #walk#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was standing by the #latch# already. | The #piglet# came when I called.
line @1 preclose : The #piglets# need one last count before dark. | The #bells# will be too early tomorrow.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #grandmother# would have found that #pig# first. | The #sow# sings more nearly on key.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #trough# is full. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will look in the next #pen#.
line @1 give.advice : Close the #gate# before counting the #pigs#. | Leave clean #straw# where the #piglets# sleep.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay near the #cart# on the #road#. | Keep the #yard# #gate# shut tonight.
scene feed_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before the #pigs# crowd in, I measure their #feed#. | The small #piglets# need their share.
b : Do they get pushed out? | Who watches them?
a : The #boar# tries. | I do.

scene sow_latch
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The old #sow# knows when the #latch# has not caught. | I pull it twice before leaving the #yard#.
b : Has she escaped? | Is she clever?
a : Once. | More than the #boar#.

scene piglet_voice
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #piglet# calls differently when it is hungry or lost. | I listen before looking in the #pens#.
b : Can you tell each one? | Who taught you?
a : Most of them. | The #master# helped.

scene straw_bedding
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Clean #straw# keeps the #piglets# dry after #rain#. | I move the old bedding out before supper.
b : Do they mind? | Is it heavy work?
a : They settle in. | Less than a full #cart#.

scene boar_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #boar# pushes the #gate# when he hears the #feed# #cart#. | I bring his share last.
b : Does he wait? | Is that safe?
a : He grumbles. | With the #fence# shut.

scene herding_lesson
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learned to count #hooves# when the #pigs# hid behind the #wood#. | A moving #herd# is harder to count by heads.
b : Do you still do it? | Does it work?
a : When the #field# is crowded. | If they move slowly.

scene grandmother_judgment
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #grandmother# can tell when a #pig# is ill before a young #hand# can. | I believe the ones who have kept a #yard#.
b : Do you know many? | Do they agree with you?
a : More than I can count. | Not often.

scene grandmother_advice
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Someone told me their #grandmother# would keep the #gate# open for air. | I asked whether she also liked chasing #piglets#.
b : Were they angry? | Was she right?
a : A little. | About the air, perhaps.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# tastes better after a cold #morning# in the #yard#. | I save the thick piece for supper.
b : Do you catch it? | Do you share?
a : I buy it. | With the #house#.

scene full_larder
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full #larder# makes the #house# quieter after work. | I check it before buying #sweets# at the #festival#.
b : Do you keep count? | What runs out first?
a : Enough to know. | Usually #bread#.

scene frosty_morning
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : White #frost# lets me see the #hooves# near the #fence#. | The #pigs# hurry toward the #feed#.
b : Do your hands freeze? | Does the frost last?
a : Until I carry the #cart#. | Not all #day#.

scene early_bells
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The early #bells# sound before I have found my #boots#. | The #pigs# wake anyway, so I go out.
b : Do you mind them? | Do they help?
a : Every #morning#. | The #herd# ignores them.

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A stale #loaf# takes more work than my #trough# scoop. | I would rather eat #eel# or fresh #bread#.
b : Do you throw it away? | Who buys fresh?
a : The #pigs# may take crumbs. | Whoever reaches #market#.

scene yard_song
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sing while the #feed# falls into the #trough#. | The #sow# stops calling long enough to hear it.
b : Does she like the song? | Who taught it to you?
a : She listens. | Someone at home.

scene festival_music
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learn a #song# from the #festival# each year. | The #chorus# follows me back to the #yard#.
b : Do others sing? | Do you stay late?
a : Some #hands# join. | Until the #music# stops.

scene city_trip
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I went to the #city# thinking I would return with more #coin#. | I came back to the #yard# and kept the story short.
b : What happened? | Do you regret going?
a : Nothing worth a #song#. | I learned the #road#.

scene house_supper
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# is full of #hands# from the #yard# and #orchard#. | I can hear three #songs# before the #meal# ends.
b : Do you join in? | Is there enough food?
a : Usually. | We make sure.

story latch_escape [topic=work self.age>=12]
  : A #sow# found a loose #latch# before I did.
  : I followed her #hooves# across the frosty #field#.
  b : She knew the way. Did you catch her?
  : She came back for the #feed#.

story grandmother_gate [topic=family self.age>=12]
  : A #visitor# said their #grandmother# would leave the #gate# open.
  : The #piglets# almost took that advice first.
  b : A risky opinion. Did you close it?
  : Before they reached the #road#.

story city_return [topic=memories self.age>=12]
  : I went to the #city# hoping for a larger #coin# than yard work paid.
  : I returned to the #pigs# with little to show for it.
  ask : What went wrong?
  b : A hard trip.
  : I would rather sing about the #field#.

rule @bark_pig
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #piglet# has found the #gate#. | Bring the #feed# to this #pen#.

rule @bark_song
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say I know the next #chorus#. | The #sow# waits for the last note.

rule @bark_frost
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #frost# shows every #hoof#. | Watch the #path# by the #wood#.

rule @bark_bell
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Those #bells# are early again. | The #pigs# knew dawn was coming.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #pigs# are busy with #feed#. | #greet#. Want to hear the next #song#?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #sow# stayed behind the #gate# today. | You came back for the #chorus#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I herd #pigs# at #self.workplace#. | I fill #troughs#, clean #pens#, and count #piglets#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I have #straw# to carry. | #saying.capitalize#. Close the #gate#.
graft resident.hub
choice What does a grandmother know? -> grandmother
node grandmother
say A good one notices a sick #pig# before the rest of us do.
free
choice Will you sing something? -> song
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node song
say Hear the #chorus# as I bring #feed# to the #trough#.
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #feed# is ready. | #greet#. The #frost# is lifting.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will count the #herd#. | I will save the next #song# for another #day#.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. Come see the #piglets#. | #greet#. I know a short #song#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have #feed# to carry. | The #gate# is shut now.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I counted the #pigs# myself. | #greet#. I have the next #chorus#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #sow# is still watching. | I will bring the #cart# back.
